{"step_index":140,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:34:14Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T20:34:14+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T20:34:14+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/pipeline/known_relations.py`\nTotal Lines: 510\nTotal Bytes: 23725\nShowing lines 1 to 100\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: \"\"\"\n2: pipeline/known_relations.py — curated known relations for the novelty filter.\n3: \n4: The base table in :mod:`pipeline.novelty` speaks a small symbolic vocabulary\n5: (``alpha``, ``gamma``, ``omega``, …) and covers the classical chains\n6: (Whitney, König–Egerváry, Gallai, …). This module *extends* it with a large,\n7: domain-curated list of known graph-invariant relations over the **domination**\n8: and **zero-forcing** families (``total_domination_number``,\n9: ``zero_forcing_number``, ``annihilation_number``, ``slater``, …) that the base\n10: table does not name — the relations a graph theorist already considers folklore\n11: or published, so that a CEGIS survivor restating one of them is flagged\n12: *known* rather than *novel*.\n13: \n14: The relations are kept here as **human-readable strings** (exactly the form a\n15: domain expert writes them), and parsed at import time into the\n16: ``(lhs, {rhs: coeff}, offset, class, name)`` tuples that\n17: ``pipeline.novelty.KNOWN_THEOREMS`` consumes. Parsing is deliberately\n18: conservative: anything that does not parse cleanly to a linear relation over the\n19: known vocabulary (nonlinear ``ceil`` forms, multi-class hypotheses, unsupported\n20: \"not K_n\" / degree-bounded hypotheses, malformed fragments) is **skipped** and\n21: left *novel* — the safe direction, since wrongly hiding a real conjecture is the\n22: only error that matters here.\n23: \"\"\"\n24: from __future__ import annotations\n25: \n26: import logging\n27: import re\n28: from collections import defaultdict\n29: from typing import Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n30: \n31: logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n32: \n33: # A KNOWN_THEOREMS entry:  (lhs, {rhs_inv: coeff, ...}, offset, class|None, name)\n34: Tuple5 = Tuple[str, Dict[str, float], float, Optional[str], str]\n35: \n36: # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n37: # Invariant vocabulary.  Tokens (graphcalc-style column names, plus a couple of\n38: # common spellings) map to the symbolic names used inside the novelty table.\n39: # The classical invariants reuse the base table's short names so the new\n40: # relations *compose* with the existing ones through the LP; the domination /\n41: # zero-forcing family invariants are new and map to themselves.\n42: # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n43: \n44: TOKEN2SYM: Dict[str, str] = {\n45:     \"order\": \"n\", \"size\": \"m\",\n46:     \"max_degree\": \"Delta\", \"maximum_degree\": \"Delta\",\n47:     \"min_degree\": \"delta\", \"minimum_degree\": \"delta\",\n48:     \"average_degree\": \"avg_deg\",\n49:     \"clique_number\": \"omega\", \"independence_number\": \"alpha\",\n50:     \"chromatic_number\": \"chi\",\n51:     \"domination_number\": \"gamma\", \"independent_domination_number\": \"ind_dom\",\n52:     \"vertex_cover_number\": \"vertex_cover\", \"matching_number\": \"nu\",\n53:     \"diameter\": \"diam\", \"radius\": \"rad\",\n54: }\n55: \n56: _NEW_INVARIANTS = [\n57:     # domination family\n58:     \"total_domination_number\", \"connected_domination_number\",\n59:     \"restrained_domination_number\", \"outer_connected_domination_number\",\n60:     \"roman_domination_number\", \"double_roman_domination_number\",\n61:     \"two_rainbow_domination_number\", \"three_rainbow_domination_number\",\n62:     \"power_domination_number\", \"sub_total_domination_number\",\n63:     \"edge_domination_number\",\n64:     # independence / matching / cover extras\n65:     \"annihilation_number\", \"residue\", \"square_residue\",\n66:     \"slater\", \"LG_sl